WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.379
We trust experts, but that doesn't always

00:00:07.379 --> 00:00:09.240
work out, especially in the field of

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.750
education policy. Back in 2001, Congress

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.269
passed the No Child Left Behind Act. Set

00:00:15.269 --> 00:00:16.740
the ambitious goal that a hundred

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.539
percent of our nation's students would

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:20.189
be reading and doing math on grade level

00:00:20.189 --> 00:00:23.250
by 2014. Didn't work out. We didn't even

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.519
come close, but along the way we actually

00:00:26.519 --> 00:00:29.429
did some real harm. Schools got over-focused

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.560
on testing; kids got caught up in

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.690
drill-and-kill assignment; and parents got

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.030
concerned that schools forgot a lot of

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.370
what matters for a kid's education. Or take

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.079
the Obama administration's School

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:42.629
Improvement Grants program. Seven billion

00:00:42.629 --> 00:00:46.020
dollars later, a 2017 federal evaluation

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.820
found that the program made no

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.320
difference for kids in participating

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.199
schools. Expertise has a role to play, but

00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:54.539
experts only know a little bit about

00:00:54.539 --> 00:00:56.730
what actually goes on in complicated

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.770
schools and among the complexities of

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.260
education policy. That's why you'd do well

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.449
to take advice from any of us experts

00:01:03.449 --> 00:01:06.340
with more than a few grains of salt.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.380
To learn more about my take on school

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:10.950
reform, check the links in the

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.320
description below. Also, let us know what

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.750
other topics you'd like AEI scholars to

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:19.130
cover in 60 seconds.

